---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About" description="About NanophotonicsLab — browser-based nanophotonics simulation tools created by José Ramón Martínez Saavedra.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>About</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about-content">

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2>What is NanophotonicsLab</h2>
        <p>
          NanophotonicsLab is a collection of browser-based tools for nanophotonics,
          optical scattering, plasmonics, electron microscopy, wave optics and ultrafast
          laser calculations.
        </p>
        <p>
          All numerical tools run entirely in your browser. There is no server-side
          computation — your data never leaves your device. Some tools use
          <a href="https://pyodide.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pyodide</a>
          to run Python scientific libraries (NumPy, SciPy) client-side via WebAssembly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2>Who made this</h2>
        <p>
          Created and maintained by
          <strong>José Ramón Martínez Saavedra</strong> — physicist with a background
          in theoretical nanophotonics and experience in scientific software, photonics
          and deep-tech product development.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2>Intent and limitations</h2>
        <p>
          The tools are intended for exploration, teaching, rapid estimation and
          reproducible numerical checks. They are <strong>not</strong> a substitute
          for full electromagnetic simulation workflows or peer-reviewed validation
          in critical designs.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each tool documents its numerical model, assumptions and references.
          Where approximations are used, they are stated explicitly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2>Technical details</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Built with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Astro</a>, vanilla TypeScript and Pyodide</li>
          <li>All computation is client-side — no backend, no accounts, no tracking cookies</li>
          <li>Analytics via <a href="https://umami.is" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Umami</a> (privacy-friendly, no cookies, no personal data)</li>
          <li>Source code: <a href="https://github.com/nanophotonicslab-com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/nanophotonicslab-com</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For bug reports, feature requests or questions:
          <a href="mailto:info@nanophotonicslab.com">info@nanophotonicslab.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: calc(var(--space-3xl) + var(--space-lg)) 0 var(--space-xl);
    background: var(--bg-soft);
  }

  .page-hero h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .about-content {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .about-block {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .about-block h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .about-block p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .about-block p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .about-block ul {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    padding-left: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .about-block li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .about-block a {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .about-block a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
